Shadowfetch Welcome catalog
===========================

Static, root-owned JSON records - one file per catalog entry, named
<id>.json with the file name matching the record's "id" field.  These
records are the single source both the Welcome assistant (Ignition page,
media and preset cards) and Control Center > Software & Updates > Bundles
render from. Local models are owned by Buzz's native Compute workflow, not
by catalog records or a second Shadowfetch model installer.

Schema (all keys always present):

  id          lowercase [a-z0-9-], matches the file name
  name        display name for the card
  kind        apt | preset | template
  packages    Debian package names (apt/preset only; [] otherwise)
  url         reserved; null or empty in every 3.0.0 record
  sha256      reserved; null or empty in every 3.0.0 record
  size_bytes  download size.  For apt/preset entries this is the
              named-package sum ("at least"); the ISO build pipeline runs
              apt-get -s in the build chroot and merges the measured
              closure over these numbers via sizes.json (judge fold: cards
              never print estimated closures)
  license     plain-words license shown on the card
  min_ram_gb  reserved; 0 or null in 3.0.0 records
  requires    [] of gates: "none", "nvidia" (shown only when the firstboot
              GPU-detect flow found NVIDIA), "btrfs"
  blurb       honest card copy - sizes, speed expectations, caveats

Rules inherited from the 2.1.2 spec:

  * apt/preset entries install through pkexec
    /usr/libexec/shadowfetch-bundle-install <id> - a single apt
    transaction against the pinned snapshot + umbra mirrors, wrapped in
    Phoenix Points by the 79phoenix-space + 80snapper DPkg hooks.
    Bundles contain ONLY pinned-snapshot Debian packages, never umbra
    packages, so an offline-saved choice resolves identically forever.
  * Model selection and download are intentionally outside this catalog.
    Buzz ranks compatible open models for the detected hardware and downloads
    the user's selection when shared compute is enabled.
  * Nothing in the catalog phones home. apt installs happen only after the
    user confirms and go to the configured mirrors.
